    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <FlexiPage> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
         "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

         THE NDAs RELATED LIST (identifier ndasList) WAS ADDED 2026-08-09 UNDER DECISION D20/C2,
         AND IT IS A WORKING SURFACE, NOT DECORATION. D19.1 makes the stage-entry trigger create
         the BUYER NDA only; the INTRODUCING BROKER's NDA is, in D19.1's own words, "added from
         the related list". There was no related list on this page and DPEG_Disposition_Edit
         carried allowCreate=false on NDA__c, so that sentence described a workflow no
         disposition persona could perform. D20/C2 grants allowCreate; this list is the other
         half of the same fix and neither half works without the other.

         relatedListApiName IS NDAs__r - the relationshipName on NDA__c.Disposition__c is "NDAs",
         and the child-relationship form used by force:relatedListSingleContainer appends __r.
         Precedent in this repo: Lease_Activities__r, Renewal_Activities__r.

         DELIBERATELY IN main, NOT IN THE SIDEBAR TABSET. The sidebar tabset holds a single
         Activity tab; adding a second tab would bury the New button one click deep, and being
         able to ADD the broker's NDA is the entire reason this component exists.

         DELIBERATELY CARRIES NO VISIBILITY RULE. NDAs are collected on OFF-MARKET dispositions
         only, so it is tempting to scope this to that record type. It is not scoped, for two
         reasons: an on-market disposition simply has zero NDAs and renders an empty list, which
         costs nothing; and record-type picklist restriction is UI-ONLY, so an on-market row CAN
         receive an NDA by API, seed or data load - in which case hiding the list would hide the
         evidence rather than prevent the cause. Showing it is the honest failure mode.

         ⚠ THE NEW BUTTON NEEDS NO RECORD-TYPE CHOOSER: DPEG_Disposition_Edit's
         recordTypeVisibilities expose exactly one NDA type, Disposition_NDA, so creation from
         here applies it without prompting. If a second disposition NDA type is ever added, a
         chooser appears and this assumption has to be revisited.

         ⚠ CLICKING THROUGH FROM THIS LIST INSIDE THE DISPOSITION APP DEPENDS ON A SECOND FILE:
         applications/Disposition.app-meta.xml carries a View actionOverride for NDA__c pointing
         at NDA_Record_Page, added in the same change. Without it the NDA opens on whichever page
         the org assigns, which is where the Advance Stage and Mark Declined buttons are NOT.

         =====================================================================
         2026-08-10 (code review 3B/3C, C1 half 2) - THE OTHER TWO LISTS OF DESIGN 4.8 ADDED:
         loisList (LOIs__r) AND contractReviewsList (Contract_Reviews__r).
         =====================================================================
         Design 4.8 required THREE related lists here. Only the NDA one shipped, so a disposition
         LOI and a disposition PSA had no read surface AND no creation route on the parent that
         defines them - the same shape as the NDA gap D20/C2 closed, twice over. Both new lists
         sit in `main` alongside ndasList, and the two pre-existing visibility rules
         (c_dispositionMain, flexipage_fieldSection) are UNTOUCHED, exactly as 4.8 required:
         adding items alongside them is additive and cannot blank the region.

         relatedListApiName IS THE CHILD RELATIONSHIP NAME + __r, read off the field files rather
         than guessed: LOI__c.Disposition__c has relationshipName LOIs, and
         Contract_Review__c.Disposition__c has relationshipName Contract_Reviews. Note the second
         is NOT "ContractReviews" - the underscore is real and a silent typo here renders an
         empty component rather than an error.

         🔴 NEITHER NEW LIST CARRIES A VISIBILITY RULE, AND THAT IS A DELIBERATE DEVIATION FROM
         DESIGN 4.8, WHICH ASKED FOR LOI AT Disposition_Stage__c = 'LOI' AND CONTRACT REVIEW AT
         'PSA'. Three reasons, and the third is the decisive one:
           1. CONSISTENCY. ndasList already carries none. Three sibling lists that appear and
              disappear under three different rules make the page unreadable.
           2. THE SCOPE ARGUMENT THAT JUSTIFIED ndasList DOES NOT EVEN APPLY HERE. NDA is an
              OFF-MARKET-ONLY stage, so an on-market disposition genuinely never reaches it.
              LOI and PSA are on BOTH record types' Disposition_Stage__c value sets (verified in
              objects/Disposition__c/recordTypes/), so there is no record-type story at all.
           3. 🔴 A STAGE-SCOPED LIST HIDES A RECORD THAT STILL EXISTS. Stage is a MOVING value:
              the moment a deal advances LOI -> PSA, an LOI-scoped list would hide the LOI that
              was just negotiated, and at Closing both lists would vanish while the executed PSA
              is precisely the document a closer needs. A related list scoped to the stage that
              CREATED the child is only correct if the child stops mattering when the stage
              moves, which is the opposite of true here. That is the same failure mode ndasList's
              own note rejects one paragraph up: hiding the list hides the evidence.
         The cost accepted in exchange is an EMPTY list on a disposition still at Readiness. That
         is cheap and self-explanatory; an invisible LOI is neither.

         ⚠ THE NEW BUTTON ON THESE TWO LISTS IS CURRENTLY INERT AND THAT IS BY DESIGN, NOT A BUG
         TO CHASE ON THIS PAGE. DPEG_Disposition_Edit holds allowCreate = FALSE on both LOI__c and
         Contract_Review__c because creation belongs to D16.2 stage-entry auto-create
         (DispositionStageEntryService, Apex, developer-owned). These lists are therefore the READ
         surface plus the recovery route if allowCreate is ever granted; they are not the creation
         route the way ndasList is. See DPEG_Disposition_Edit's own in-root note, corrected in the
         same change - it previously justified withholding allowCreate on an auto-create that had
         not been built.

         ⚠ SAME actionOverride DEPENDENCY AS ndasList: clicking through from either new list
         inside the Disposition app needs a View actionOverride for LOI__c and Contract_Review__c
         in applications/Disposition.app-meta.xml pointing at LOI_Record_Page and
         Contract_Review_Record_Page. Without them the record opens on whichever page the org
         assigns - which is where the Advance Stage buttons are NOT, making the C3 fix on
         Contract_Review_Record_Page unreachable from here. -->

